# The film's timing — the beat table's one machine-read home.
#
# One BEATDRIFT row per seed, verbatim as `probes/CensusBeatDrift` printed it, at the tree
# the row's own `sha=` names. `probes/bench.sh` hands this file to the probe with
# --baseline-file, so the judged row compares today's ticks against these and the sweep goes
# red the moment a beat moves at all: the band is 0 since #1002, so these rows are a pin and
# not a tolerance, and the only way past a red sweep is re-measuring them here.
#
# Blank lines and lines opening with `#` are ignored. Every other line must open with
# `BEATDRIFT ` and must carry the `ticks=` the sweep runs at: a row measured at another
# budget is refused rather than compared, because two budgets are two questions and the
# difference would report itself as drift.
#
# Moving the pin is these rows re-measured, in the commit that moves the film, with the sha
# they were measured at riding in the rows themselves. `git log -p -- probes/beatdrift.baseline`
# is then the whole move history, kept by git, which cannot drift from the value it explains —
# the discipline .github/canonical-digest already keeps for the seal. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's
# census entry 2 keeps the narrative table of recorded commits and the per-step verdicts; this
# file is the row the bench actually reads.
#
# Re-measure from a pinned tree (D-030 clause 3 — an exported tree has no .git to ask, which
# is what --sha is for):
#
#     git archive <sha> | tar -x -C "$WORK" && cd "$WORK"
#     javac -encoding UTF-8 --release 17 -d out $(find src -name '*.java')
#     javac -encoding UTF-8 --release 17 -cp out -d probes/out probes/*.java
#     java -cp out:probes/out CensusBeatDrift 42,7 6000 --sha <short>

# Moved by #377 (the Room 303 unwriting). A mind who was going to die does not, and the
# whole back half of the film slides with him: at seed 42 overflow, flatline, peace, reboot
# and the door all come 254 ticks early and the second Thomas 240 early; at seed 7 the same
# five arrive 213 late and the second birth 220 late. Both directions, because the clause
# does not delay the cascade — it changes who is standing in it. Six of the eight beats at
# each seed cleared the declared 200-tick band, which is the band doing its job: this is a
# declared move and not drift. Was sha=a7660c2 (overflow 4289 / 3707). The band was 200 when
# that move was judged; it is 0 from the rows below down.
#
# Re-measured by #1002 at 8f41b30, main's head, and unchanged tick for tick — the film has not
# moved since #377's export, so this commit moves the band and not the rows. The band it moves
# is the one docs/ARCHITECTURE.md census entry 2 declared and never measured. Here is the
# measurement: across the 142 commits from 0cad45b (entry 2's last recorded row) to a7660c2
# (the pin #377 replaced) the film drifted ten ticks — seed 42's second birth, with overflow,
# flatline, peace, reboot and the door one tick early apiece, and seed 7 not moving at all —
# and the row judging that slide said DRIFT_WITHIN_BAND, with no reading in between because
# nothing in the tree ever recorded one. A band twenty times a drift it was pointed at is not
# a tolerance, it is silence: it prints the identical line over a tree that did not move and
# over one that moved 199 ticks. Entry 2's table holds the other half of the argument — seed
# 7's beats slid 119 ticks between 2b49550 and 62e12ac and that step is recorded as
# WITHIN_BAND, so the largest undeclared move on record was absorbed with no reason written
# anywhere. And seed 7 has no other witness in this repository at all, since
# the canonical seal watches seed 42 alone. At 0 a beat that slides one tick re-pins here with
# its reason attached, which is what .github/canonical-digest has always demanded of the seal.
BEATDRIFT sha=8f41b30 seed=42 ticks=6000 birth=1299 refusal=1525 overflow=4035 flatline=4035 peace=4055 reboot=4075 door=4075 second_birth=4989 max_delta=n/a
BEATDRIFT sha=8f41b30 seed=7 ticks=6000 birth=1259 refusal=1525 overflow=3920 flatline=3920 peace=3940 reboot=3960 door=3960 second_birth=4879 max_delta=n/a
